+# LangChain & RAG Integration (Aegis)
+
+Overview
+- This document describes how to use the LangChain adapter and the FAISS embedding utilities included in Aegis.
+
+Quick start (dev)
+1. Install requirements for integrations:
+   pip install -r ops/integrations/requirements-langchain.txt
+2. Generate proto stubs (if not already done):
+   python3 ops/grpc/_generate_stubs.py
+3. Build small sample dataset and index:
+   python3 tools/data/build_sample_dataset.py
+   python3 -c "from ops.integrations.embeddings_faiss import build_index; build_index(open('data/sample_texts.txt').read().splitlines())"
+4. Start the inference server (HF or vLLM if available):
+   USE_VLLM=false python3 ops/grpc/inference_server_vllm.py
+5. Run the RAG demo:
+   python3 services/agents/langchain_rag_demo.py
+
+LangChain integration
+- If `langchain` is installed, `ops.integrations.langchain_llm.GenerationLLM` subclasses LangChain's LLM interface so you can use it directly with LangChain chains.
+- `ops.integrations.langchain_tools.make_all_tools()` returns LangChain Tool wrappers (when langchain is available) for the built-in agent tools. These wrappers enforce runtime safety via safety_monitor.
+
+Embedding & FAISS
+- `ops.integrations.embeddings_faiss` provides build_index() and query_index() helpers using sentence-transformers and faiss.
+
+LangGraph adapter
+- `ops.integrations.langgraph_adapter.execute_graph_plan()` runs a simple graph plan mapping nodes to tools. Use this to integrate graph planners (LangGraph or others).
+
+Notes
+- vLLM requires CUDA and system dependencies — only install vllm in dedicated GPU inference nodes.
+- Adjust model names via env vars (HF_MODEL, VLLM_MODEL) and set USE_VLLM=1 to prefer vLLM.
+- For production, replace demo tokenizer and toy models with production models, and add batching, backpressure, auth and rate-limiting.
+
